WEBVTT

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:05.570
Is this a monster?

00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:06.550
Or is it...

00:00:06.550 --> 00:00:08.470
I... I don't know...

00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:09.410
Father?

00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:10.110
What?

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:12.480
D-Did she just say "Father"?

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:15.590
No... Why did this happen?

00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:16.510
Don't!

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:18.160
Yuusuke?!

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:21.590
I heard from the other
players we contacted online

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:23.650
that there's a parasite called a wireworm

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:25.580
that parasitizes other creatures'
brains to control them.

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:28.430
So that thing is feeding on him?

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:30.440
You can't kill them by
cutting or crushing them.

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:32.820
The best way is to burn them
along with their host.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:33.550
Burn...

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:34.770
No!

00:00:34.990 --> 00:00:36.500
Let me go!

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:38.400
The moment that thing attached to his brain,

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:40.800
he was already dead.

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:46.110
I'm sorry, but we can't let
our whole party be wiped out.

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:47.410
Yuusuke...

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:48.950
Shit!

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:52.480
Glen-san!

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:54.030
Hakozaki-san, cut it off!

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:00.960
Hey!

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:10.830
F-Father...

00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:13.680
No! Don't!

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:24.690
What happened?!

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:28.320
Oh... Tokitate-san, perfect timing.

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:29.070
Huh?

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:32.310
Would you mind burning him?

00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:37.360
Why do I have to do this?

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:39.950
If you don't burn the body
as soon as possible,

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:43.140
it can apparently progress
into a pandemic very quickly.

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:45.750
Father...

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:54.940
Jezby!

00:01:55.960 --> 00:01:57.150
Jezby!

00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:34.860
Looks like she just lost consciousness.

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:39.640
Why didn't you bring the sword down?

00:03:40.050 --> 00:03:43.560
I tried to... but I couldn't.

00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:46.730
How can you be so calm about this?

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:49.610
This isn't the time to
talk about being calm.

00:03:49.610 --> 00:03:52.960
The monsters have gotten stronger,
and we need to get used to it.

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:56.940
We came close to losing
Glen-san right off the bat.

00:03:57.910 --> 00:03:59.740
What are you talking about, Yuusuke?

00:03:59.740 --> 00:04:01.430
Kusue's reaction is correct.

00:04:01.430 --> 00:04:02.170
Huh?

00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:05.990
He may have been taken over by
a parasite, but he was human.

00:04:05.990 --> 00:04:06.970
Not only that...

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:10.890
I lost my grasp on my sensibility.

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:13.240
Getting used to this is what's abnormal.

00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:16.450
Hakozaki-san...

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:20.740
From now on, if you don't think
you can do something, say so.

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:22.920
I'll handle tasks like this.

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:27.290
I've already killed a man, after all.

00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:29.640
Yotsuya-kun...

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:33.990
Though I didn't realize at the
time that this world was real...

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:37.430
But it doesn't matter. I'm already tainted.

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:40.670
You don't want to see things like
that, do you, Hakozaki-san?

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:43.100
I don't.

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:45.970
I don't, but...

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:49.160
If someone has to do this no matter what...

00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:52.010
If the same thing has to happen
whether I watch or not...

00:04:52.010 --> 00:04:55.690
That won't make it okay that I
was the only one not looking!

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:59.600
You try to bear too much
weight alone, Kusue.

00:04:59.850 --> 00:05:01.930
I don't like dead bodies, either.

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:05.290
There was a time when I almost
became depressed because of it.

00:05:05.290 --> 00:05:08.570
U-Um... Did you say "dead bodies"?

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:11.250
There's such a thing as the
right person for the job.

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:12.500
You're ignoring me?

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:16.410
There are hundreds of thousands of things
that must be done in this world.

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:20.650
Why should you force yourself to
do one that you're not good at?

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:24.140
A hidden passage?

00:05:24.370 --> 00:05:25.260
Yes.

00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:27.640
The entrance is just ahead.

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:32.670
What made her suddenly decide
to take us there, though?

00:05:32.670 --> 00:05:35.360
It must've been... what happened yesterday.

00:05:36.130 --> 00:05:40.430
Also, we still haven't been told
any details at all, have we?

00:05:42.850 --> 00:05:44.270
Everyone, this is it.

00:05:46.530 --> 00:05:48.580
Ooh, it opened!

00:05:48.920 --> 00:05:50.920
It looks pretty deep.

00:05:55.300 --> 00:05:57.070
A limestone cave?

00:06:04.390 --> 00:06:05.980
Say, Jezby...

00:06:06.770 --> 00:06:08.850
How much farther is it to the village?

00:06:08.850 --> 00:06:11.710
About... half a day.

00:06:11.710 --> 00:06:13.110
Half a day?!

00:06:13.110 --> 00:06:15.990
I wish you had told us that sooner...

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:17.510
Also...

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:19.830
If we fall, we're dead, aren't we?

00:06:19.830 --> 00:06:23.680
And if a strong monster showed
up here, we'd be goners.

00:06:25.910 --> 00:06:27.520
Vampire bats?

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:28.540
I knew it!

00:06:28.540 --> 00:06:30.940
They're even weaker than goblins.

00:06:30.940 --> 00:06:33.010
This time, I'll take care of it!

00:06:33.010 --> 00:06:34.760
Okay, they're all yours.

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:35.360
Huh?

00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:38.040
These guys might be stronger now, too.

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:39.370
Be careful.

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:41.860
Huh? Hey, wait a—

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:49.820
Let's take a break here.

00:06:50.740 --> 00:06:53.440
D-Damn it, you guys...

00:06:53.630 --> 00:06:56.140
I'm glad you got some experience out of it.

00:06:56.950 --> 00:06:58.360
The Journey of Hope?

00:06:58.360 --> 00:07:01.590
A chosen few leave the village to search

00:07:01.590 --> 00:07:05.170
for a place where we can
all live more safely.

00:07:05.450 --> 00:07:07.520
My father was one of them.

00:07:07.520 --> 00:07:08.970
Why would they do that?

00:07:09.460 --> 00:07:12.870
The monsters that attack
us have gotten stronger,

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:15.680
and every year, we're able to
harvest fewer and fewer crops.

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:21.520
The village chief said we couldn't keep
living in this village much longer.

00:07:21.930 --> 00:07:25.220
So the monsters have
definitely gotten stronger.

00:07:25.380 --> 00:07:29.140
Normally, it's older people who are chosen.

00:07:29.140 --> 00:07:31.750
Since they can't do their jobs anymore,

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:35.880
the idea is that they can at
least help the village that way.

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:37.440
What sort of reasoning is that?

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:39.340
That's just harsh, man.

00:07:39.340 --> 00:07:41.520
Fewer mouths to feed, huh?

00:07:41.920 --> 00:07:46.440
I've heard of the same thing happening in
poor mountain villages in Japan long ago, but...

00:07:46.830 --> 00:07:51.050
That's why the villagers
call the Journey of Hope

00:07:51.050 --> 00:07:53.600
"the Journey of Death" in secret.

00:07:55.110 --> 00:07:58.300
My father and a young man named Dan

00:07:58.300 --> 00:08:02.560
tried to convince the village chief
that we shouldn't do this anymore,

00:08:03.220 --> 00:08:06.090
but the chief listed a bunch
of reasons to keep doing it,

00:08:06.510 --> 00:08:11.220
so the two of them ended up being
sent on the Journey of Hope anyway.

00:08:11.650 --> 00:08:15.190
After that, my mother fell ill...

00:08:15.630 --> 00:08:20.330
It was just me and my little brother,
and we didn't know what to do...

00:08:20.870 --> 00:08:24.230
So I left the village to
bring our father back home.

00:08:25.300 --> 00:08:28.500
I happened to stumble upon the
shack Father had been living in,

00:08:29.150 --> 00:08:32.850
but he said he couldn't break the rules.

00:08:33.490 --> 00:08:38.370
Not only that, but I would probably
be executed for bringing him back.

00:08:39.400 --> 00:08:45.000
The next day, Father left, saying he was
going to talk to the village chief.

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:46.340
I never saw him again.

00:08:46.340 --> 00:08:49.970
So when you said you thought
we were from the village...

00:08:49.970 --> 00:08:52.170
I thought he had failed
to convince the chief

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:55.660
and the villagers had come to get me.

00:08:55.660 --> 00:09:00.550
But not only did he never come
back, he ended up like that...

00:09:02.340 --> 00:09:05.940
What about the man who left
the village with your father?

00:09:07.050 --> 00:09:08.780
By the time I got here,

00:09:08.780 --> 00:09:10.760
he was already gone.

00:09:10.760 --> 00:09:15.310
Father said he went to find a place
called New Eden somewhere in the world.

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:16.980
New Eden?

00:09:16.980 --> 00:09:18.870
I don't know anything about it.

00:09:19.150 --> 00:09:22.960
My father was against it,
but he couldn't stop him...

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:25.300
and Dan never came back.

00:09:25.530 --> 00:09:29.050
Wait, Jez-chan... Isn't it a bad
idea for you to go to the village?

00:09:29.240 --> 00:09:31.370
Didn't you say they might execute you?

00:09:32.350 --> 00:09:38.150
But I need to tell my mother and
brother that Father is dead.

00:09:42.890 --> 00:09:44.960
We're almost at the entrance to the village.

00:09:45.330 --> 00:09:47.850
We don't want the chief's
friends to find us,

00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:49.660
so I'll scout ahead.

00:09:49.660 --> 00:09:51.300
I'll go with you.

00:09:51.300 --> 00:09:52.290
That's all right.

00:09:52.290 --> 00:09:55.510
I'll just take a look outside,
and then I'll be right back.

00:09:56.660 --> 00:10:01.250
Our quest was to stop the village
of Zagroth from being destroyed,

00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:04.410
but it doesn't seem like it's
in imminent danger, does it?

00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:08.200
Maybe there's some hidden <i>something</i>
that could destroy it?

00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:12.330
There's no telling what might happen. Right?

00:10:12.330 --> 00:10:16.600
But I do think I'm starting
to see what we need to do.

00:10:16.600 --> 00:10:18.770
Nobody's there! Now's our chance!

00:10:18.770 --> 00:10:23.270
We need to make sure Jezby isn't executed
upon returning to the village.

00:10:23.270 --> 00:10:24.570
Right.

00:10:33.490 --> 00:10:35.070
So this is...

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:37.610
the village of Zagroth.

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:51.380
Looks like the population might
only be a hundred or so.

00:10:51.780 --> 00:10:55.780
You'd be just barely squeaking
by if you had to live here.

00:10:56.160 --> 00:10:57.330
Who are you people?!

00:11:00.040 --> 00:11:01.320
Heroes?

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:03.350
Are you really heroes?

00:11:03.610 --> 00:11:05.190
What are you doing here?

00:11:05.190 --> 00:11:06.270
Froc!

00:11:06.270 --> 00:11:08.600
J-Jezby?

00:11:10.610 --> 00:11:13.140
You're... alive?

00:11:13.430 --> 00:11:14.700
Are they friends?

00:11:15.060 --> 00:11:17.140
Looks like they're closer than that.

00:11:17.660 --> 00:11:19.820
He's my neighbor. We grew up together.

00:11:19.820 --> 00:11:23.150
You just vanished without warning.
What were you thinking?

00:11:23.150 --> 00:11:25.930
I left to tell Father about Mother...

00:11:25.930 --> 00:11:28.490
Oh, how are my mother and Lanan?

00:11:30.370 --> 00:11:31.680
Froc?

00:11:32.890 --> 00:11:35.360
Milady, we should really head back now.

00:11:35.580 --> 00:11:37.170
It's starting to get dark.

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:38.020
No!

00:11:38.590 --> 00:11:41.460
I'm going to find that flying monster today!

00:11:41.460 --> 00:11:42.710
Milady!

00:11:42.710 --> 00:11:44.230
Please wait!

00:11:44.580 --> 00:11:46.130
Let her do what she wants.

00:11:46.130 --> 00:11:47.170
But...

00:11:47.530 --> 00:11:49.430
It's the same thing as always.

00:11:49.430 --> 00:11:52.530
She's lying and dragging us
around for her own jollies.

00:11:55.220 --> 00:11:56.220
No...

00:11:56.730 --> 00:11:59.070
I don't believe it... When?

00:11:59.770 --> 00:12:00.910
Two days ago.

00:12:01.690 --> 00:12:03.630
Her condition suddenly got worse...

00:12:03.630 --> 00:12:05.850
M-Mother...

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:07.650
Mother...

00:12:08.610 --> 00:12:09.980
Mother!

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:17.370
Froc, where is Lanan?

00:12:17.870 --> 00:12:20.320
At my house, but...

00:12:21.250 --> 00:12:22.960
Wait here. I'll bring him.

00:12:26.070 --> 00:12:27.080
Lanan?

00:12:29.060 --> 00:12:32.080
Lanan... Hey, Lanan?

00:12:32.080 --> 00:12:34.340
Don't you recognize me?

00:12:35.040 --> 00:12:38.520
He's been like this since your mom died.

00:12:39.270 --> 00:12:41.420
He won't talk to anyone,

00:12:41.420 --> 00:12:43.430
and he doesn't answer when
anyone talks to him.

00:12:43.430 --> 00:12:46.620
Lanan, please! Answer me!

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:50.340
It's probably from the shock
of watching his mother die.

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:53.900
I'm going to take a look around the village.

00:12:53.900 --> 00:12:55.160
I'll go with you.

00:12:55.160 --> 00:12:55.660
Huh?

00:12:56.100 --> 00:12:57.200
Problem with that?

00:12:57.430 --> 00:12:58.910
N-No...

00:13:00.750 --> 00:13:04.060
This definitely doesn't seem
like an easy place to live.

00:13:04.770 --> 00:13:07.720
Do you think they had a reason to
cling to this place so tightly

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:11.880
that they'd reduce their own numbers by
sending people on the Journey of Hope?

00:13:12.480 --> 00:13:14.260
I think I get it.

00:13:15.270 --> 00:13:19.460
When you've lived so long in a place like
this, where it feels like time has stopped...

00:13:20.840 --> 00:13:24.670
Before you know it, you can no longer escape.

00:13:25.250 --> 00:13:26.360
You think so?

00:13:27.080 --> 00:13:31.790
Sometimes the only way to
move forward is to escape.

00:13:32.020 --> 00:13:34.510
As if she understands anything...

00:13:34.510 --> 00:13:36.020
I'm surprised, though.

00:13:36.630 --> 00:13:38.030
By what?

00:13:38.030 --> 00:13:41.100
You came out here because it
hurt you to watch Jezby, right?

00:13:41.100 --> 00:13:41.700
Huh?

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:47.500
I thought you were a lot more stoic.

00:13:47.840 --> 00:13:50.680
I think it's closer to regret, actually.

00:13:51.080 --> 00:13:52.260
Regret?

00:13:52.260 --> 00:13:54.850
If we had gotten here just a little sooner,

00:13:55.350 --> 00:14:00.950
maybe I could've saved Jezby's
mother with my creature magic.

00:14:01.690 --> 00:14:04.320
If you start thinking like that,
there'll be no end to it.

00:14:04.760 --> 00:14:06.000
You're right.

00:14:07.690 --> 00:14:08.820
Someone's coming.

00:14:14.240 --> 00:14:15.280
Milady!

00:14:16.760 --> 00:14:17.890
Hi there.

00:14:17.890 --> 00:14:19.000
Hello.

00:14:19.200 --> 00:14:22.410
Why did you come to this village?

00:14:22.410 --> 00:14:26.080
Uh, we... um...

00:14:26.520 --> 00:14:29.630
Please don't, milady. These people are...

00:14:29.630 --> 00:14:31.240
Yes, I know!

00:14:31.240 --> 00:14:35.090
And I'll have you know that this
village doesn't need heroes!

00:14:35.870 --> 00:14:38.760
Well, thank you for the warm welcome.

00:14:38.760 --> 00:14:42.410
If there are any problems,
Grandfather will make them all better!

00:14:43.710 --> 00:14:45.450
Wait, are you...

00:14:45.450 --> 00:14:47.890
I'm Iris DiRaio.

00:14:47.890 --> 00:14:50.360
Don't take that condescending tone with me.

00:14:50.790 --> 00:14:53.910
I do apologize, Miss Iris.

00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:55.010
"Miss"?

00:14:55.010 --> 00:14:58.700
Gosh... No one's ever
called me that before...

00:14:58.990 --> 00:15:03.030
Um... By any chance, is this
young lady's grandfather...

00:15:03.620 --> 00:15:08.090
Yes, he is the village chief, Cox DiRaio.

00:15:10.280 --> 00:15:13.550
So you're Dan's younger brother?

00:15:14.050 --> 00:15:18.050
So Bayne is dead and my
brother is missing? Damn it!

00:15:18.050 --> 00:15:21.490
That stupid village chief thinks
that just because he's old,

00:15:21.490 --> 00:15:23.970
our village needs him or whatever,

00:15:23.970 --> 00:15:25.920
so he never leaves it himself.

00:15:26.150 --> 00:15:29.900
But he'll make up his own selfish reasons
to send anyone inconvenient to him

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:33.860
on the Journey of Hope,
regardless of their age.

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:39.570
Well, if it isn't the great heroes!

00:15:39.770 --> 00:15:45.750
I had heard rumors of great heroes who
traveled the world saving people,

00:15:46.190 --> 00:15:49.460
but I never would have expected
them to visit this remote village.

00:15:49.460 --> 00:15:50.880
What an honor!

00:15:51.290 --> 00:15:52.550
However...

00:15:52.550 --> 00:15:54.880
I'm afraid you've wasted your time.

00:15:55.240 --> 00:15:56.720
What do you mean?

00:15:57.030 --> 00:15:58.630
Oh, nothing.

00:15:58.630 --> 00:16:01.630
It's just that Zagroth is
the very image of peace,

00:16:01.630 --> 00:16:07.290
so there is nothing here for which we
require the aid of the great heroes.

00:16:07.290 --> 00:16:10.980
Perhaps you would be better
off trying elsewhere.

00:16:10.980 --> 00:16:13.230
Is he trying to get rid of us?

00:16:13.470 --> 00:16:14.640
Wait a moment.

00:16:15.020 --> 00:16:20.240
Um... I heard you've had frequent
attacks by unusually strong monsters.

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:23.760
Could you please let us
protect this village?

00:16:23.760 --> 00:16:25.000
Don't, Yuusuke!

00:16:26.550 --> 00:16:29.580
And who told you this?

00:16:29.580 --> 00:16:30.800
Oh, crap...

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:35.460
I can't tell him about Jezby
before I know what he might do.

00:16:35.460 --> 00:16:36.680
It was Jezby.

00:16:38.250 --> 00:16:42.440
I saw her walking with them.

00:16:42.690 --> 00:16:45.890
I see. So it was Jezby...

00:16:47.190 --> 00:16:51.030
I did feel terrible for what
I did to that poor girl.

00:16:51.440 --> 00:16:54.890
Even if it was to help the village,
I took her from her father,

00:16:54.890 --> 00:16:57.480
with no way of knowing that her
mother would die, as well...

00:16:57.930 --> 00:17:00.890
I'm so grateful that she
returned to the village.

00:17:01.360 --> 00:17:05.300
And as for the monsters, you need not worry.

00:17:05.300 --> 00:17:07.940
We have a secret plan, you see.

00:17:07.940 --> 00:17:08.890
You do?

00:17:08.890 --> 00:17:10.050
Yes, we do!

00:17:10.050 --> 00:17:13.020
And I would love to show it to you.

00:17:14.040 --> 00:17:17.460
It may be of some help to you
in your future exploits.

00:17:17.460 --> 00:17:19.760
Ah, perhaps I've said too much.

00:17:27.170 --> 00:17:28.470
Great Heroes.

00:17:31.030 --> 00:17:32.150
Over there.

00:17:32.760 --> 00:17:35.690
Please take this opportunity
to give it a close look.

00:17:36.170 --> 00:17:38.370
I can't imagine it being
anything that special,

00:17:38.780 --> 00:17:41.650
but it wouldn't benefit us to
take an attitude with him here.

00:17:41.650 --> 00:17:42.520
Yeah.

00:17:47.850 --> 00:17:49.810
Um, is this it?

00:17:52.270 --> 00:17:53.170
You bastard!

00:17:53.170 --> 00:17:55.900
Do forgive me, Great Heroes.

00:17:55.900 --> 00:17:58.960
You are a greater threat
to me than any monsters.

00:17:59.410 --> 00:18:01.880
But I do thank you

00:18:01.880 --> 00:18:06.250
for bringing back the scoundrel
who broke the rules.

00:18:07.240 --> 00:18:08.890
What are you gonna do to Jezby?!

00:18:09.120 --> 00:18:11.170
What would that knowledge do for you?

00:18:11.170 --> 00:18:14.450
You two won't be leaving
here until you're dead.

00:18:14.650 --> 00:18:15.730
What?!

00:18:16.510 --> 00:18:20.340
I've heard that heroes can come
back to life when they die.

00:18:20.340 --> 00:18:23.210
But if I leave you in there for a year,

00:18:23.410 --> 00:18:25.800
I'm sure you'll finally wither away.

00:18:26.020 --> 00:18:27.850
Wait! Chief!

00:18:29.920 --> 00:18:31.890
What... is this?

00:18:31.890 --> 00:18:34.510
Frog eggs from the pond out back.

00:18:34.510 --> 00:18:35.550
Ew!

00:18:35.550 --> 00:18:38.640
I'm sorry we can't offer anything special.

00:18:38.640 --> 00:18:41.480
N-No, really, there's no
need to trouble yourself...

00:18:41.680 --> 00:18:43.630
Ever since that happened,

00:18:43.630 --> 00:18:47.380
we've had little contact with
the rest of the villagers.

00:18:47.900 --> 00:18:51.310
Our family and Jezby's
are treated as outcasts.

00:18:52.030 --> 00:18:55.280
They're even making me work
outside the village as a guard.

00:18:55.710 --> 00:18:58.240
All because the chief wanted
to make an example of us...

00:18:58.240 --> 00:19:01.000
Oh, so that's why you were out there.

00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:03.830
Anyway, what's taking those two so long?

00:19:03.830 --> 00:19:05.560
Maybe something happened...

00:19:06.170 --> 00:19:07.650
Oh, there they are.

00:19:08.220 --> 00:19:09.570
Village Chief!

00:19:11.150 --> 00:19:12.430
That's him?

00:19:13.250 --> 00:19:15.700
I'm sorry to drop in so late.

00:19:15.700 --> 00:19:19.060
But you see, two heroes
just paid me a visit...

00:19:19.470 --> 00:19:23.340
What's this? There are more heroes here?

00:19:23.340 --> 00:19:26.020
Well, well, what a surprise!

00:19:26.020 --> 00:19:27.910
Are you here to take Jezby?!

00:19:28.550 --> 00:19:29.920
No, Froc!

00:19:29.920 --> 00:19:31.180
Relax.

00:19:31.400 --> 00:19:34.370
I've come here per the heroes' request.

00:19:35.050 --> 00:19:37.610
They asked me to forgive Jezby.

00:19:38.350 --> 00:19:41.410
I guess the two of them
managed to convince him.

00:19:41.410 --> 00:19:43.710
Jeez, they said they were
just gonna look around,

00:19:43.710 --> 00:19:45.500
but they got the jump on us like that?

00:19:45.500 --> 00:19:47.980
And... where are they now?

00:19:47.980 --> 00:19:48.790
Hmm?

00:19:48.790 --> 00:19:53.830
Oh, the heroes are at my mansion.

00:19:53.830 --> 00:19:56.390
I've ensured that they are being served
the finest meal we could offer.

00:19:56.390 --> 00:19:57.760
A meal...

00:19:57.760 --> 00:19:59.720
You are all welcome to join them if you—

00:19:59.720 --> 00:20:00.480
We're in!

00:20:00.740 --> 00:20:01.800
Jezby...

00:20:02.330 --> 00:20:04.270
According to our rules,
it sets a poor example

00:20:04.640 --> 00:20:09.370
if those who leave the village without
permission are not harshly punished,

00:20:09.710 --> 00:20:13.680
but if it is the heroes' wish,
the villagers will surely agree.

00:20:14.530 --> 00:20:16.950
You can tell your story
in more detail later.

00:20:16.950 --> 00:20:19.540
For tonight, you and your brother
should get plenty of rest.

00:20:19.540 --> 00:20:21.600
Now, shall we go, Great Heroes?

00:20:21.600 --> 00:20:22.630
'Kay!

00:20:22.630 --> 00:20:25.740
Iu-chan, Kusue-chan, let's get going.

00:20:26.050 --> 00:20:27.360
S-Sure...

00:20:27.550 --> 00:20:29.520
Something seems shady about all this...

00:20:30.260 --> 00:20:32.790
But I guess just sitting
around won't do any good.

00:20:35.400 --> 00:20:38.650
Once I've left with the
heroes, capture Jezby.

00:20:38.650 --> 00:20:39.380
Yes, sir.

00:20:38.810 --> 00:20:39.380
Yes, sir.

00:20:39.660 --> 00:20:42.370
Who would have thought there
were more heroes here?

00:20:47.290 --> 00:20:48.380
It's not working.

00:20:50.060 --> 00:20:51.290
Yuusuke?

00:20:51.290 --> 00:20:54.670
I'm sorry. This happened
because I told him too much.

00:20:54.670 --> 00:20:56.350
It was my fault.

00:20:58.730 --> 00:20:59.940
Help me!

00:20:59.940 --> 00:21:01.920
What are you doing?! Stop!

00:21:02.750 --> 00:21:04.030
Froc!

00:21:07.710 --> 00:21:09.700
Hey! Where do you think you're grabbing?!

00:21:09.700 --> 00:21:10.830
Oops, sorry.

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:12.910
Please do be careful.

00:21:13.250 --> 00:21:16.420
Um, Chief, is your mansion...

00:21:18.660 --> 00:21:20.880
It's beyond that forest.

00:21:20.880 --> 00:21:23.370
I apologize for making you walk so far.

00:21:23.790 --> 00:21:24.820
What is it?

00:21:25.240 --> 00:21:27.600
I truly do apologize.

00:21:30.490 --> 00:21:31.770
I'm slipping!

00:21:31.770 --> 00:21:32.880
What the hell are you doing?!

00:21:33.170 --> 00:21:38.550
Now I don't need to go through the trouble of
locking you in the dungeon, like the other two.

00:21:38.550 --> 00:21:39.900
Dungeon?!

00:21:39.900 --> 00:21:43.270
Yes. The bog beneath you
is bottomless, you see.

00:21:43.270 --> 00:21:44.610
Once you fall, it's all over.

00:21:45.010 --> 00:21:47.150
Even monsters never make it back out.

00:21:47.660 --> 00:21:49.240
Not for all eternity.

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:26.670
Next week on <i>Million Lives</i>...

00:23:26.670 --> 00:23:28.420
"Draining All the Water from the Well,"

00:23:28.420 --> 00:23:30.750
"Discovery of the Legendary Non-Native
Species, the Basilisk!?"

00:23:30.750 --> 00:23:33.680
and "A Super Huge Monster
Appears!" Three altogeth.

00:23:33.880 --> 00:23:35.980
Don't miss next week's episo!

00:23:35.980 --> 00:23:37.650
Rock, paper, scissors!

00:23:37.960 --> 00:23:38.680
Bye!
